{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790372935,"nonce":"ubNIC69uuT4/iVPElH0iZ/iKRkA=","title":"Loop scalar replacement aborts on a loop variable that starts null","message":"This program aborts the process (exit 134, \"scalar root without a definition\" in sroa_loop.rs, inside a function that cannot unwind), in the default and cranelift-only builds, and in every NUC binary back to f610b68 (2026-09-20):\n\n    class Point {\n      construct new(x) { _x = x }\n      x { _x }\n    }\n    class Bench {\n      static builds() {\n        var p = null\n        var i = 0\n        while (i \u003c 400000) {\n          p = Point.new(i)\n          i = i + 1\n        }\n        return p.x\n      }\n    }\n    System.print(Bench.builds())\n\nThe null reaches the loop header through a parameter of the preheader: bb0 -\u003e bb4(v26 = null) -\u003e bb1(v3). The seeding drops v26 (fed a non-scalar), but v3 was already given Point's class from the back edge (v14 = Point.new), and a feed from a candidate parameter only marks \"class unknown\", so v3 stays a scalar parameter after v26 is dropped. The escape check only looked at scalar arguments flowing into non-scalar parameters, not the reverse, so the rewrite asked for v26's fields and hit the unreachable.\n\nFound while writing an e2e test for 01f1cae.","files":null}]}